    "slug": "nine-somali-detainees-transferred-from-guant-namo-to-somalia",
    "summary": "The United States has repatriated nine Somali men from the Guantánamo Bay detention facility to Somalia, including three individuals from Minnesota. The transfer follows nearly a month of detention at the U.S. naval base in Cuba.",
    "content": "The United States has transferred nine Somali men from the Guantánamo Bay detention facility in Cuba to Somalia, according to immigration authorities. The group, which included three individuals from Minnesota, was flown on a private aircraft last week. Among those repatriated were Adam Mohamed Abdullah and Hassan Abtidoon.\n\nThe men had been held for approximately one month at the U.S. detention facilities in Guantánamo before being sent to Somalia. Interviews conducted at Guantánamo indicate that the detainees reported being mistreated by officers from the immigration agency. The circumstances leading to their detention and subsequent transfer have not been fully detailed by U.S. officials.\n\nGuantánamo Bay has long been used by the United States to hold individuals outside of standard legal jurisdictions, a practice that has drawn criticism from human rights organizations. The transfer of Somali nationals from the facility is part of ongoing U.S. immigration enforcement operations. The specific reasons for their detention and the legal processes involved remain unclear.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, particularly in Minnesota, which hosts one of the largest Somali communities in the United States, this transfer raises concerns about the treatment of community members in U.S. custody. Families and advocacy groups have previously voiced worries about the lack of transparency and due process for Somali detainees. The return of these individuals to Somalia may also prompt questions about reintegration and the conditions they will face upon arrival.\n\nThe Somali government has not issued a public statement regarding the transfer. It is also unknown whether the men will face any legal proceedings in Somalia or if they will be allowed to return to their families. The Minnesota-based Somali community continues to seek information about the detained individuals and their well-being.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/03/sagaal-soomaali-ah-oo-guantanamo-lagu-hayay-ayaa-loo-soo-masaafuriyey-soomaaliya/",
